IT:
{{TAG:0003:0012:}}{{TAG:0007:000B:}}Caspitina!{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}} Che faccia!{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
Sembra una pagnotta!
Ti ha punto un'ape?

ES:
{{TAG:0003:0029:}}¡Ay, qué mala suerte!{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}} Tienes pinta
de que te haya picado una abeja.{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
{{TAG:0003:0009:}}¿Te duele mucho?

IT:
{{TAG:0003:0029:}}Oh, no!{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}} Deve averti punto un'ape!{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
Scommetto che fa malissimo!
Poverin{{TAG:000E:0006:02006F0002006100}}!

DE:
{{TAG:0003:000D:}}Auweia, das sieht ja schlimm aus!{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
Mir tut das Gesicht weh, wenn ich
dich nur angucke,{{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}} {{TAG:0005:0007:}}.

EN:
I've been stung before too,{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}} so I
know how rough it can be.{{TAG:0000:0004:}}{{TAG:0003:0001:}}But {{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}it'll get better if you just wait.{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
So don't get too down, {{TAG:0005:0008:}}.

IT:
{{TAG:0003:0000:}}Mi piace la tua nuova faccia.{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}
Ti dà un certo carattere!{{TAG:0000:0004:}}Se però non sei alla ricerca
di un look "faccia da pagnotta",{{TAG:0007:0000:14000000}}{{TAG:0007:0000:08000000}}
prendi questa, {{TAG:0005:0007:}}!
